Joeb wrote:
>   I have a few questions for the knowledgeable posters here:
>
> 1.  Is there a way to proof armor besides ?oEA or ?oDA?  I don't think
> so, but I want to be sure.

Not that I'm aware of.  Also, I'm not aware of any way to repair
damaged armor short of confused enchant armor--once it's rusty, it's
rusty.  In my opinion, this is an oversight; oil will repair weapons,
so why can't we repair armor?

> 2. If I dip a pile of !oH in a single !oS I get a pile of diluted !oEH.
>  If I then dip that pile of diluted !oEH in a !oGL or a !oGE will I get
> a pile of diluted !oFH  or will something bad happen?  Can I do it
> again and get a pile of diluted !oGA?

Alchemy with diluted potions is fine, and works just like non-diluted
potions.  So yes, you can get those extra heals up to gain
ability--something I do in most of my games (that make it that far, of
course!)

> 3.  What happens if I wear water walking boots on the Plane of Water
> and try to walk on water?  I hear that doesn't work but it seems like
> it should.

You get wet.  I did that on my last ascension--I had Vlad's
water-walking boots fireproofed, which worked great for the plane of
fire, but didn't help on the plain of water, to my surprise.  I agree,
this feels wrong to me.  (Actually, what feels more wrong is being able
to levitate outside of the bubble; if the entire plane is water, it
shouldn't be possible to get "above" it.)

